ers, the former NC State and NFL star quarterback, had been coaching high school football for six years.","published":"2026-11-19T12:19:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514617/philip-rivers-nc-state-fairhope-alabama","type":"Story","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Game Day Kickoff: Appreciating Jeremiah Smith's greatness","description":"What to expect in Week 12, from top games and players to teams on upset alert.","published":"2026-11-19T17:08:28.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/page/gamedaykickoff111926/week-12-top-games-upsets-preview","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Inside the complexities of clock management in college football","description":"From Michigan-WMU to Notre Dame-BYU, the closing seconds of games seem to be more puzzling than ever.","published":"2026-11-19T12:17:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50522229/the-complexities-clock-management-college-football","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4921108/desean-bishop","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeSean_Bishop"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"DeSean Bishop","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeSean_Bishop","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:30Z","intro":"DeSean Bishop (born October 15, 2004) is an American college football running back for the Tennessee Volunteers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Bishop played running back for Karns High School where he recorded 8,347 rushing yards and 102 rushing touchdowns. On July 14, 2022, Bishop committed to continue his playing career at Coastal Carolina, but decommitted after head coach Jamey Chadwell was hired by Liberty. On December 21, 2022, Bishop decided to join the Tennessee Volunteers as a preferred walk-on."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"During his true freshman year, Bishop did not play in any games and took a redshirt after suffering an injury during the preseason.\nDuring the 2024 season, Bishop served as the second-string running back behind All-SEC selection Dylan Sampson. Despite facing injuries in the later weeks of the season, Bishop was able to accumulate 455 yards and three touchdowns on 74 carries.\nIn January 2025, Bishop was given a football scholarship. He finished the 2025 season with 182 carries for 1,076 rushing yards and 16 rushing touchdowns."}]}}